# TEXT RECOGNITION, FOR THE DEMONSTRATION SERVICE ONLY. BD-21, answered.
#
# Append these to /etc/eje-staging/eje.env — NOT to /etc/eje/eje.env.
#
# CONFIRM THE ISOLATION BEFORE PROCESSING ANYTHING, which is what the mandate
# asks and what this file cannot do for you. The staging unit has its own user,
# port, database and storage directory (`docs/vps-staging.md`), and all three of
# these must be true before the first document is read:
#
#   systemctl cat eje-staging | grep -E 'User=|EnvironmentFile='
#   sudo -u eje-staging env | grep -E 'EJE_DATABASE_URL|EJE_STORAGE_DIR'
#   # the database name and the storage path must BOTH differ from the
#   # production unit's, and `npm run preflight` must report
#   # deployment=staging rather than production.
#
# Recognition reads and rewrites the library's index, so a staging unit pointed
# at the production database would be the demonstration quietly editing EJE's
# real library — the one failure this separation exists to prevent.
#
# The owner answered BD-21 (#63) on 23 October 2026: configure local OCR in the
# DEMONSTRATION environment first, and measure before deciding about production.
# This file is the demonstration half of that answer, kept separate from
# `eje.env.example` so it cannot be pasted into a production environment file
# by accident.
#
# WHAT IT COSTS, MEASURED rather than estimated: 23 to 25 seconds of CPU per A4
# page at 300 dpi, on a four-core machine. See docs/library-ocr.md §5 for the
# method, both samples and the consequence — in short, a 214-page manual is
# about an hour and a half and is partially indexed under these defaults.
#
# INSTALL FIRST, or every job settles as "no engine":
#
#   sudo apt-get install -y tesseract-ocr tesseract-ocr-eng poppler-utils
#
# `tesseract-ocr-eng` is listed separately on purpose: the `tesseract-ocr`
# package does not always pull the English trained data, and without it every
# page fails. The application reports that case as "the eng language data is not
# installed" rather than as an unreadable scan.
EJE_OCR=local

# THE DEFAULTS ARE LEFT ALONE DELIBERATELY. Raising either of the two limits
# below is a decision about how much of the VPS one document may occupy, and it
# is the decision the measurement exists to inform — not something to change
# while setting the demonstration up.
#
# EJE_OCR_MAX_PAGES=40
# EJE_OCR_DEADLINE_MINUTES=20

# AFTER STARTING, confirm the binaries are really there:
#
#   sudo -u eje-staging npm run library:ocr -- --report
#   sudo -u eje-staging npm run library:ocr -- --max 5
#
# `npm run preflight` warns if EJE_OCR=local is ever set on a deployment that
# declares itself production, which is not what BD-21 asked for.
